[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#Loki","page":"API","text":"Loki\n\nAn interactive environment for time-series analysis built on CausalFrames: a graph of CausalPipelines and time-series operators, diagnostics over every node's output, and export of the graph as a plain Julia script. See DESIGN.md.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Loki"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#Loki.Acausal","page":"API","text":"Loki.Acausal\n\nLoki's forward-looking operators, the counterpart of CausalFrames.Acausal. Nothing here is re-exported from Loki: using an operator whose output at time t depends on rows after t takes an explicit using Loki.Acausal.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Loki.Acausal"},{"category":"section","location":"#Loki.jl","page":"Home","text":"An interactive environment for time-series analysis built on CausalFrames. You build a graph of CausalPipelines and time-series operators (differencing, EMA, MACD, AR, ARMA, …), inspect each node's output through diagnostics such as ACF, PACF and residual tests, and export the graph as a plain Julia script. The same session can be driven from a browser or by an agent over MCP.\n\nLoki is under construction; DESIGN.md describes the design and its milestones.","title":"Loki.jl"}]
